    m_ResultText: "SubstepCost_ScalesLinearly (0,011s)\n---\n  400 substeps took 4,008 ms against 2,123 ms for 100 \u2014 a ratio of 1,89 where 4 was expected. Well below 4 means significant fixed cost per call. Well above, on a mobile device, most likely means the two runs were scheduled onto different core clusters rather than anything about the kernel.\n  Expected: 4.0d +/- 2.0d\n  But was:  1.8875388527832719d\n\n---\nat Project.Physics.Tests.KernelThroughputTests.SubstepCost_ScalesLinearly () [0x00000] in <00000000000000000000000000000000>:0"
